            "review_title": "Review at Oc Oanh",
            "review_text": "vdollero\nLondon, United Kingdom47 contributions\n0\nDisappointing Experience - Hygiene Concerns\nDec 2025 • Family\nI visited Ốc Oanh based on an AI recommendation that claimed this restaurant had Michelin recognition. Given what I experienced, I seriously doubt any such recognition exists.\nHygiene Issues:\n\nThe most concerning incident was witnessing a staff member use the restroom without washing their hands before returning to serve customers. The kitchen facilities appeared outdated and didn't seem to follow basic sanitary standards. Overall cleanliness was well below acceptable levels.\n\nFood Quality:\nThe octopus had good flavour but was served warm rather than hot, which raised additional food safety concerns given the hygiene issues observed.\n\nValue:\nWhile prices are lower than Western standards, they weren't particularly cheap considering the condition of the establishment and service standards.\n\nFinal Thoughts:\nI'm genuinely surprised that AI systems are recommending this place, and I question the accuracy of any claimed Michelin recognition. The hygiene standards alone would disqualify it from any reputable dining guide. There are many excellent, clean local restaurants in Ho Chi Minh City at similar or better price points—I strongly suggest looking elsewhere.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nOctopus and shrimp were ok. Scallops with cheese were rubbery and inedible\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten December 27, 2025",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
